30,2,1,talk,Rin,,"It takes up to nine minutes just to get screens working upstairs! Also, people arrive at totally different times, from eight to ten.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"We are billed by area, not people, so empty desks still cost us. Plus, every single power move costs 6,200 yen per desk.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The current plan leaves three people without windows, which was a huge complaint. Also, unplanned shuffles caused weeks of interruptions.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The printer area is much noisier than the windows. Also, the physio says it takes days of tweaking to get a workstation comfortable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Sitting together meant handover notes disappeared because people just asked across the aisle. New joiners also learned faster by overhearing us.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if moving desks costs money every time, maybe we shouldn't move them often?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Toshio,,Exactly. Frequent changes would be a financial drain on a budget that hasn't increased.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, if it takes days to get comfortable, a system where we move constantly sounds like a nightmare.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shion,,I agree. Constant readjustment of monitor arms and chairs would be exhausting and inefficient.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Yumi,,But we lose so much knowledge if we are too spread out. The social side is a huge productivity boost.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, but if we have to spend ten minutes every morning setting up, that's a lot of wasted gaps in my day!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, the cost of empty space is already high. We can't afford a layout that is inefficient or requires constant paid rewiring.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, the badge records show that a first-come-first-served system would be decided before half the team even arrives.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shion,,The noise difference is significant. Some of us need the quiet window side to actually focus.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, if we just assign seats by function, we might keep the project strands together and help the new people.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
