55,3,1,talk,Rin,,Free Address sounds like a waste of time every morning and unfair for late arrivals. I'm against A.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Rotating Blocks would be a financial disaster with those rewiring quotes. I can't support B.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Fixed Desks by Function avoids the chaos of unplanned shuffles and lets us address the window issue fairly.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shion,,I need a stable spot to keep my physio settings and avoid the printer noise. Fixed is the only way.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Fixed Desks by Function lets us group project teams together, which we know helps the joiners and the workflow.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Rin,,"If we go with Fixed, we don't waste those precious morning minutes plugging things in. I'm for C.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Toshio,,C is the most budget-friendly since we only pay for the power setup once. I vote C.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, as long as we decide who gets the windows logically, C is the most stable choice.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shion,,I'll vote C. It's the only option that respects the physical need for a settled workstation.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I agree. The benefits of proximity for the team outweigh the variety of rotating. I vote C.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
